card.statement:
(a) The set of Kronecker canonical forms of all pairs in a sufficiently small neighborhood of

\begin{equation}
\mc L^T_m \oplus
\mc L^T_n,\qquad m\le n
\end{equation}

consists of the pairs

\begin{equation}
\mc L^T_{m+r} \oplus
\mc L^T_{n-r},\qquad m+r\le n-r,\ r\ge 0.
\end{equation}

(b) Each pair <<ref:u5g>> with $r>0$ is equivalent to a pair of the form

\begin{equation}
\left(
\mat{L^T_m&0\\0&L^T_n},
\mat{R^T_m&\D_r(\varepsilon)
\\0&R^T_n}
\right)
\end{equation}

(which is obtained by an arbitrarily small perturbation of <<ref:(1)>>), in which $\D_r(\varepsilon )$ is defined in <<ref:rdpd>> and $\varepsilon$ is an arbitrary nonzero complex number.
